  "title": "Check: Lines of Best Fit (B)",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "multiple-choice",
      "difficulty": "knowledge-check",
      "stem": "A line of best fit passes through the point $(20, 35)$ and $(40, 55)$. Use it to estimate the $y$-value when $x = 30$.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$40$"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$45$"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$50$"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$42.5$"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "b",
      "explanation": "The gradient is $\\frac{55-35}{40-20} = \\frac{20}{20} = 1$. At $x = 30$ (halfway between $20$ and $40$), $y = 35 + 1 \\times (30 - 20) = 35 + 10 = 45$."
    }
  ]
